# Conventional Commits (English only)

All commit messages must be **English** and follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/).

## Format

```
<type>(optional-scope): <short summary>

[optional body]
```

- Summary: imperative mood, lowercase after the type, no trailing period
- Keep the subject ~72 chars or less
- Body explains **why** when needed, not a file dump

## Common types

| Type | Use for |
|------|---------|
| `feat` | New user-facing feature |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `refactor` | Code change that is not a fix or feature |
| `test` | Adding or updating tests |
| `chore` | Maintenance (deps, tooling, agent rules) |
| `style` | Formatting / whitespace (no logic change) |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `ci` | CI/CD config |
| `build` | Build system or bundler config |
| `revert` | Revert a previous commit |

## Examples

```
feat: add user login page
fix: resolve null pointer crash in cart
docs: update readme installation steps
refactor: clean up user auth service
test: add unit tests for payment module
chore: update package dependencies
perf: cache pricelist generation results
ci: add typecheck job to github actions
build: enable next standalone output
style: format nest module imports
```

## Scopes (optional)

Use when it clarifies the area: `web`, `api`, `i18n`, `docker`, `agent`.

```
feat(i18n): add language switcher
chore(agent): add conventional commits rule
```

## Do not

- Write commit messages in Russian or mixed languages
- Use vague subjects (`update`, `fix stuff`, `wip`)
- Bundle unrelated changes in one commit when they can be split cleanly
